#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""finalize-run recovery contract (Plan.CS.v2.1 §4).

The two tests the plan makes part of the op's definition, plus the pending
alert and the tick seam:
  concurrent   two finalizers on one run dir: one row, one evidence record,
               one finalized.json; the loser reports pending, never finalized
  kill-retry   FINALIZE_RUN_CRASH_AFTER each of check|transcript|publish|row,
               then a retry: the original check.json verdict is kept (the
               workspace is broken in between so a rerun would fail), no
               second row or record, finalization completes
  estate       missing ESTATE refuses the row -> pending
               raises exactly one finalization_pending alert whose age grows
               across evaluations and never resets; the third retry (ESTATE
               restored) clears it
  publish      publish-evidence failure keeps the row, records finalize.error,
               leaves finalized.json absent; the retry publishes, no second row
  marker       complete manifest present, ready_for_inspection absent (the crash
               window inside publish-evidence): the retry re-publishes the
               marker and finalizes; both present, or an incomplete capture's
               manifest (never marked): the retry calls publish-evidence never
  mismatch     check.json whose stimulus_sha differs from terminal.json's (or is
               empty against a frozen one): pending, reason names both hashes,
               nothing appended; a matching file is reused, never rerun
  env          the check inherits only the runner's child allowlist
  v2 row: the appended row is row_version 2; a clean run has no
               error and no call_errors; finalized.json names error_class
  envelope     the outbox holds <run_id>.json binding the row and every file by
               sha256; a kill after it and a retry reuse it; a tampered envelope
               is pending and never overwritten
  enospc       ENOSPC before the row writes finalize.error class spool_full, the
               alert shows it; the retry after space returns appends one v2 row
  durable      terminal.json and the run dir are fsync'd on entry, before any
               step, and the outputs are those of an unobserved run
  tick         a runner exit 3 yields a dispatch TERMINAL row with
               stop finalization_pending, code 3, whether no row landed
               (estate) or the finalizer's row did and publish failed
               (publish); completion is withheld; the next tick's sweep
               finishes the dir and appends nothing twice; (publish) a
               later tick's age sweep removes an old report cell dir no run
               can claim and keeps a young one, one whose report cwd is a
               pending run's workspace, and one holding a torn report

Template: one real run dir, produced by the runner (default Rust) with a stub
finalize-run that exits 3 (terminal.json and messages.jsonl on disk, no
transcript.md: the op renders it, nothing finalized). Every test copies the template estate. Isolated
estates only; cs/ledger is never written. $CS_RUNNER_BIN overrides the
default Rust runner.
"""
